  "speechText": "Synchronous code blocks the JavaScript thread until it finishes. With await on a database call, the current async function pauses, but the event loop can handle other callbacks while the I O is pending. When the result is ready, the function continues. Await does not move a CPU-heavy calculation off the main thread; I would use a worker thread for that.",
